@{
    Layout = "_LayoutLanding";
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "How Hermes collects, uses, stores, protects, and deletes personal and financial data.";
}

<div class="legal-content">
    <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index" class="inline-link legal-back">← Back to Hermes</a>

    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Last updated: 24 September 2026</p>

    <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how Hermes collects, uses, stores, protects, retains,
        and deletes personal data. By creating an account or using Hermes, you agree to
        the processing described below.
    </p>

    <h2>Data controller</h2>
    <p>
        Hermes is operated by Francisco Costa.
    </p>
    <p>
        Privacy and data-protection requests can be submitted through the
        <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/franciscocosta4/Hermes" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hermes GitHub repository</a>.
        Do not post passwords, credentials, or sensitive financial details publicly.
    </p>

    <h2>Data we collect</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Account data:</strong> full name, username, email address, and password credentials.</li>
        <li><strong>Financial data:</strong> income, expenses, descriptions, amounts, dates, categories, monthly budgets, and savings goals.</li>
        <li><strong>Security and technical data:</strong> authentication events, rate-limiting records, error logs, IP address, browser information, and device information.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use data</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Create, maintain, and secure your account.</li>
        <li>Store and display your financial records.</li>
        <li>Calculate balances, averages, budgets, savings progress, and overspending alerts.</li>
        <li>Provide transaction search, pagination, and CSV exports.</li>
        <li>Prevent fraud, abuse, unauthorized access, and service disruption.</li>
        <li>Respond to support, privacy, and security requests.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Legal bases</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Contract:</strong> processing necessary to provide your account and requested features.</li>
        <li><strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> security, fraud prevention, service reliability, and product improvement.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal obligation:</strong> retention or disclosure required by applicable law.</li>
        <li><strong>Consent:</strong> where optional processing requires consent under applicable law.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data sharing and processors</h2>
    <p>
        Hermes does not sell personal data and does not use advertising trackers.
        Personal data may be processed by infrastructure providers necessary to operate Hermes,
        including database, hosting, backup, and content-delivery providers.
    </p>
    <p>
        Some pages may load fonts, icons, or libraries from third-party content-delivery networks.
        Those providers may receive technical information such as your IP address, browser type,
        and requested resource.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
        Hermes uses strictly necessary cookies for authentication, session management, and security.
        It does not currently use advertising or analytics cookies. You can control cookies through
        your browser settings, but disabling essential cookies may prevent sign-in and access to
        your account.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Account and financial data are retained while your account remains active.</li>
        <li>Deleted transactions are removed from the operational database.</li>
        <li>Security logs are retained only as long as necessary for security and troubleshooting.</li>
        <li>Backup copies may persist for a limited operational recovery period before being overwritten.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
        Subject to applicable law, you may request access to your personal data, correction of
        inaccurate data, export of your data, restriction of processing, objection to processing,
        and deletion of your account and associated personal data.
    </p>
    <p>
        You can export transactions to CSV from the dashboard. For broader access, correction,
        export, or deletion requests, use the
        <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/franciscocosta4/Hermes" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hermes GitHub repository</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        Where the GDPR applies, you also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory
        authority, including the Portuguese Data Protection Authority, the CNPD.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
        Hermes is not directed to children. Accounts may only be created by people who are at
        least 16 years old or who meet the applicable minimum age in their jurisdiction.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
        This policy may be updated when Hermes features, infrastructure, or legal requirements change.
        The revised version will be published on this page with an updated revision date.
    </p>
</div>
